 "text": "Hey, nice to hear from you. How are you? A sketch is a quick drawing or painting, usually done quickly for fun. A study, on the other hand, is a more detailed drawing or painting of one subject. Kind of. It usually done for an art class or competition, and it can take weeks or months. That sounds fun. Do you want start with a quick pencil sketch, or grab few colors and make it a quick study? The big picture first, then the little details. Start with the sky, then add the mountains, and finally the trees and shrubs. I' love to hear how it turns out.",
